From 6d0ce063a491ba3337ee6a1c0ade282501008581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marks-jhojan <153632015+marks-jhojan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] runtime: UNDS event bus (UDP) for external controller
 companions

With UNDS_EVENTS=host:port the runtime publishes, as one compact JSON
datagram per event (protocol v1, integers only), what the game does with
the controller and the audio, so an external program can drive DualSense
adaptive triggers, haptics and the light bar:

  hello   at start and every 1 s: executable (u1/u2/u3), image base, pid,
          counters, open audio ports
  bye     before LoadExec (_exit 101), guest exit, restart, window close
  rumble  scePadSetVibration motors, on change (+0.5 s refresh)
  led     light bar colour, on change
  pad     the state the game read, on change (8 ms limit; buttons never
          held back; stick deadband 2)
  aopen   audio port opened
  audio   per port, 512-frame windows (10.7 ms): RMS, peak and 150 Hz
          low-passed RMS of the converted buffer; silence refreshed 1/s

Sends are non-blocking (numeric IPv4 only, no DNS), made outside the pad
lock; their duration is measured and reported. Without UNDS_EVENTS every
hook is one relaxed atomic load and nothing is printed.

UNDS_RUMBLE=0 stops scePadSetVibration from driving SDL rumble (the
event is still published): SDL rumble and a companion's haptics share the
DualSense actuators.

tests/test_unds.c covers endpoint parsing, change detection, the pad rate
limit, audio levels, seq continuity and bye (build.sh --test on Linux;
ninja -C out/gpu unds-test on Windows).
